# Supabase Configuration Example for ClassMate
# Copy this file to .env and fill in real values.
# NEVER commit .env to Git (it is already listed in .gitignore).

# ── Supabase ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-id.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=your-publishable-key

# ── Application URL (Auth Confirmation Redirects) ───────────────────────────
# In local development, leaving this unset automatically defaults to window.location.origin (e.g. http://localhost:5173).
# When deploying to production (e.g. Vercel, Netlify, Cloudflare), set this to your public HTTPS URL:
#   VITE_SITE_URL=https://classmate-web.vercel.app
#
# Supabase Dashboard URL Configuration (Authentication -> URL Configuration):
#   - Site URL: Set to your public production URL once deployed (e.g. https://classmate-web.vercel.app)
#   - Redirect URLs (Allow list):
#       http://localhost:5173/**
#       https://classmate-web.vercel.app/**
#
# VITE_SITE_URL=https://your-public-deployment-url.com


# ── Phase 3C/3D — Web Push VAPID Configuration ───────────────────────────────
#
# Generate a fresh key pair (one-time, run locally, never commit output):
#   node scripts/generate-vapid-keys.cjs
#
# The script writes VITE_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY and VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY to .env
# and prints ONLY the public key to stdout.
#
# FRONTEND (this .env file — safe to expose via Vite):
#   VITE_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY  → the base64url P-256 uncompressed public key (87 chars)
#
VITE_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=your-vapid-public-key-here

# ── Supabase Edge Function Secrets (set via Supabase Dashboard — NEVER here) ──
#
#   Navigate to: Supabase Dashboard → Settings → Edge Functions → Secrets
#
#   VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY   = <same value as VITE_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY above>
#   VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY  = *** KEEP SECRET — read from .env, never paste in chat ***
#   VAPID_SUBJECT      = mailto:you@example.com   (identifies your push server)
#   SCHEDULER_SECRET   = <a separate high-entropy random string for cron auth>
#
#   SUPABASE_URL and SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY are injected automatically by Supabase.
#
# Variable names listed here for documentation only — do NOT set real values in this file.
